[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384252145","pull_request_review_id":3275032467,"id":2384252145,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6OHMzx","diff_hunk":"@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ String OpenXRAction::get_name_with_set() const {\n \treturn action_name;\n }\n \n-void OpenXRAction::set_localized_name(const String p_localized_name) {\n+void OpenXRAction::set_localized_name(const String &p_localized_name) {\n \tlocalized_name = p_localized_name;","path":"modules/openxr/action_map/openxr_action.cpp","commit_id":"c3e6002c6e0b554c56cb2f863614be6a2672c3a8","original_commit_id":"651087c350aa408f410183b7dc0fb5243437a5e4","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is not necessarily an improvement. Or at least, it's not the best kind of improvement. I'll try to explain.\n\nIf you're taking in a reference (like `const String &`), you're forcing the callee to copy the value on use.\nHowever, another pattern is possible:\n\n\n```suggestion\nvoid OpenXRAction::set_localized_name(String p_localized_name) {\nlocalized_name = std::move(p_localized_name);\n```\n\nThis moves the responsibility to do the copy to the caller, who will sometimes need to do copies to pass into this function, but may sometimes be able to pass in 'fresh' objects, and no copy will be required at all.\n\nThis is, at least, the academic side of it. We don't have much code in Godot that uses explicit move semantics, outside of core. I think inevitably the use of explicit `std::move` will grow, especially when we start removing even more implicit conversions, and start profiling more seriously.\nSince it's so rare, I'm not sure if I'm suggesting you _actually_ use this paradigm instead of ref arguments here. But I wanted to weigh in that there is this _ideal_ reformatting that could be done instead.","created_at":"2025-09-27T17:18:29Z","updated_at":"2025-09-27T17:20:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110948#discussion_r2384252145","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110948","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384252145"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110948#discussion_r2384252145"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110948"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384252145/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":77,"original_start_line":77,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":78,"original_line":78,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":6,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384256195","pull_request_review_id":3275037134,"id":2384256195,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6OHNzD","diff_hunk":"@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ String OpenXRAction::get_name_with_set() const {\n \treturn action_name;\n }\n \n-void OpenXRAction::set_localized_name(const String p_localized_name) {\n+void OpenXRAction::set_localized_name(const String &p_localized_name) {\n \tlocalized_name = p_localized_name;","path":"modules/openxr/action_map/openxr_action.cpp","commit_id":"c3e6002c6e0b554c56cb2f863614be6a2672c3a8","original_commit_id":"651087c350aa408f410183b7dc0fb5243437a5e4","user":{"login":"aaronfranke","id":1646875,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDY4NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1646875?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke","html_url":"https://github.com/aaronfranke","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronfranke/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"That's not consistent with the existing style Godot uses throughout 99% of the codebase, which is `const Type &`. I would prefer to make this code consistent with the existing dominant way Godot handles parameters.\r\n\r\nAlso, with your proposed solution, it will always make 1 copy when the function is called. If the parameter is `const Type &` then it is possible that no copies will be made at all if the value just needs to be read or transformed without making a copy, which means 0 or 1 copies, which is better than always 1 copy IMO.","created_at":"2025-09-27T17:31:48Z","updated_at":"2025-09-27T17:31:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110948#discussion_r2384256195","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110948","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384256195"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110948#discussion_r2384256195"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110948"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384256195/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":77,"original_start_line":77,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":78,"original_line":78,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2384252145,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":6,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384257374","pull_request_review_id":3275039745,"id":2384257374,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6OHOFe","diff_hunk":"@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ String OpenXRAction::get_name_with_set() const {\n \treturn action_name;\n }\n \n-void OpenXRAction::set_localized_name(const String p_localized_name) {\n+void OpenXRAction::set_localized_name(const String &p_localized_name) {\n \tlocalized_name = p_localized_name;","path":"modules/openxr/action_map/openxr_action.cpp","commit_id":"c3e6002c6e0b554c56cb2f863614be6a2672c3a8","original_commit_id":"651087c350aa408f410183b7dc0fb5243437a5e4","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The implementation of `set_localized_name` necessitates a copy be made, because the value is assigned to `localized_name`. Whether you do the copy at the callee or at the caller site doesn't matter.\r\nThe ideal situation is that we evaluate for each function whether a ref or a copy is more appropriate for the parameter, and then implement both the callee and the caller to make the best use of this interface.\r\nHowever, that's mostly micro optimization, so I definitely won't have anyone change code over this. We _will_ have to use this paradigm in high performance APIs sooner or later, but it's not important for the majority of the codebase.","created_at":"2025-09-27T17:36:10Z","updated_at":"2025-09-27T17:36:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110948#discussion_r2384257374","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110948","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384257374"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110948#discussion_r2384257374"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110948"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2384257374/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":77,"original_start_line":77,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":78,"original_line":78,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2384252145,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":6,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/238557994